--- PrismWidget/CHUNK_1_TESTING.md
+++ PrismWidget/CHUNK_1_TESTING.md
@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+# Prism v0.19 chunk 1 — isolated binding target and honest colour preview
+
+This is an independent implementation using KWGT workflow as a user-provided reference. No KWGT proprietary bytecode/resources are included.
+
+## What changed
+- Formula sheets now bind to an immutable target (widget background or the original layer UUID + property key); the target is visible in the sheet.
+- Deleting or switching the selected item cannot silently retarget a formula.
+- Formula-bearing Paint rows show the live resolved colour and swatch, not just the original manual fallback.
+- Canvas selection no longer overlays semi-transparent accent fill on the selected shape, which had made the shape seem to change the entire backdrop.
+- Manual values remain saved. Switching to manual removes only the chosen binding.
+
+## A56 acceptance checks
+1. Make a transparent widget and TWO round rectangles with different fixed colours.
+2. Select the first rectangle > Paint > formula > Bitmap palette > Vibrant > Apply to item.
+3. Verify only first shape changes when the playing song/cover changes. Check the Paint row's Live value.
+4. Select the second shape, verify it retains its manual colour.
+5. Select no layer and edit Background independently. Neither shape should change.
+6. Disable the first binding using Use manual; first shape must return to previous fixed colour.
+7. Remove media permission or stop playback; valid manual fallback must remain visible.
+8. Repeat with FX > shadow colour and gradient end colour.
+
+Future chunks: richer text FX and music palette source selection; shared preview/launcher rendering tests; advanced group compositing.
